, 			{
				"box" : 				{
					"id" : "obj-8",
					"linecount" : 22,
					"maxclass" : "comment",
					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 643.0, 184.0, 159.0, 301.0 ],
					"text" : "jw.odot.nline\n\nThis abstraction is analogous to line or line~ but for n-element lists. For example, if one is working with 3D coordinates in x,y,z or az,elev,dist one probably wants all three values scaled at the same time. Extending this idea to n-dimensions, this gives a way of scaling quaternions and larger data structures. The abstraction accepts lists of n+1 or 2n+1 elements observing line-style syntax:\n{[a1...an], [b1...bn], t} where a is the origin and b is the target value arrived at in t milliseconds."
				}

			}
